      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the data regarding the severe national housing and affordability crisis strongly supports the *need for more supply*, definitively stating that upzoning is the *only* correct solution is an oversimplification.\n\nPro-density arguments are undeniably strong given the current under-supply, but politically and socially, there are other necessary supporting policies, like strong and consistent public investment in infrastructure, to make higher-density development truly viable and successful for the whole community.",
